    "title": "Build X (Twitter) Auto-Reply System for SaaSOptics",
    "content": "Design and deploy an automated X monitoring and reply system that tracks brand mentions, keywords, and DMs during business hours (7am-7pm ET, Mon-Fri), replies with a friendly expert tone using a standardized template, enforces a 25-reply daily cap with queuing, and exports daily CSVs for Sprout Social import.\n\n**Architecture Overview:**\n- **Language:** Python 3.11+\n- **Platform:** GitHub Actions (free tier) with scheduled workflows\n- **API:** X API v2 (Search recent tweets endpoint for keywords/mentions; DMs may require additional access)\n- **State Management:** SQLite database committed to repo for persistence across runs (tracks daily reply count and processed tweet IDs)\n- **Rate Limiting:** Hard cap at 25 replies/day with automatic queuing\n- **Output:** Daily CSV formatted for Sprout Social import\n\n**Key Components:**\n1. **Core Bot Logic:** Handles OAuth 2.0 authentication, keyword monitoring (\"SaaSOptics\", \"subscription revenue recognition\", \"ARR metrics\", #SaaSfinance), mention detection, reply composition with template (including playbook link and Megan's signature), and CSV generation.\n2. **Scheduling Infrastructure:** GitHub Actions workflow with cron triggers for business hours only (Mon-Fri, 7am-7pm ET), environment variable management for API secrets, and automated committing of state/CSV files.\n3. **Deployment Package:** Configuration templates, environment setup guide, and testing procedures.\n\n**Technical Constraints:**\n- X API v2 has rate limits (e.g., 450 requests per 15 min for search)\n- Reply cap: 25/day to avoid platform limits\n- Stateless execution environment requires git-based persistence for queue state",
